Below is a **ready‑to‑run script** that will automatically create **50 distinct SVG icons** (one for each achievement) inside your project’s `public/icons/` folder.  

Each icon follows a **Duolingo‑style flat‑cartoon look** – a rounded green circle with a unique number and a slightly different accent colour so they’re visually distinct while sharing the same overall design language.

---

## 1️⃣ Create the folder for the icons  

```bash
# From the project root (C:\Users\Anandhy\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\gk-badge-app)
mkdir public\icons
```

---

## 2️⃣ Add the generation script  

Create the file **`scripts/generate-icons.js`** with the following content (the path is absolute for your workspace):

```javascript
// scripts/generate-icons.js
// -----------------------------------------------------------
// Generates 50 Duolingo‑style SVG icons (icon1.svg … icon50.svg)
// -----------------------------------------------------------

const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

// Base colour used by Duolingo (bright green)
const baseColor = '#78C800';

// Helper to produce a slightly different hue for each icon
function getAccentColor(index) {
  // Shift hue by 7° per icon (wrap around 360)
  const hue = (index * 7) % 360;
  return `hsl(${hue}, 80%, 55%)`;
}

// SVG template – a circle with a number in the centre
function buildSvg(index) {
  const accent = getAccentColor(index);
  const size = 64; // 64 × 64 px – perfect for navigation / UI
  const fontSize = 28;

  return `<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<svg width="${size}" height="${size}" viewBox="0 0 ${size} ${size}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
  <!-- Background circle (Duolingo green) -->
  <circle cx="${size/2}" cy="${size/2}" r="${size/2 - 2}" fill="${baseColor}" />
  <!-- Accent ring -->
  <circle cx="${size/2}" cy="${size/2}" r="${size/2 - 4}" fill="none" stroke="${accent}" stroke-width="4"/>
  <!-- Number label -->
  <text x="50%" y="55%" dominant-baseline="middle" text-anchor="middle"
        font-family="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"
        font-size="${fontSize}"
        font-weight="600"
        fill="#ffffff">
    ${index}
  </text>
</svg>`;
}

// Write all 50 icons
const iconsDir = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', 'public', 'icons');
if (!fs.existsSync(iconsDir)) {
  fs.mkdirSync(iconsDir, { recursive: true });
}

for (let i = 1; i <= 50; i++) {
  const svg = buildSvg(i);
  const filename = path.join(iconsDir, `icon${i}.svg`);
  fs.writeFileSync(filename, svg, 'utf8');
  console.log(`✅ Created ${filename}`);
}

console.log('🚀 All 50 icons have been generated in public/icons/');
```

Save the file at:

```
C:\Users\Anandhy\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\gk-badge-app\scripts\generate-icons.js
```

---

## 3️⃣ Run the script  

Open a PowerShell window **inside the project folder** and execute:

```powershell
# Make sure you’re in the correct directory
cd C:\Users\Anandhy\.gemini\antigravity\scratch\gk-badge-app

# Install Node (if not already in PATH) – you already have a local node runtime,
